Let the standalone generator emit AMX GEMMs for Sapphire Rapids.

The CLI only accepted architectures up to CPX, so add `spr`, which routes BF16
GEMMs with A in VNNI-2 layout to the AMX kernel.

That kernel refused the classic ABI, which passes A, B and C in rdi, rsi and
rdx, and required the struct of the XGEMM ABI instead. The struct loads only
fill those same registers, and without the extended ABI nothing is fused, so
accept the classic ABI: open and close the inline-assembly stream the way the
AVX-512 kernels do, so it takes A, B and C rather than a `ptr` the classic
signature does not have.

The text emitter, which until now only the JIT encoder had exercised, also
labelled the tile configuration of an M remainder `.data_tconf_0` like the
first one, a duplicate symbol; give it its own id.

